KNOWNBUG
rtl-construction-clocked-blocks1.sv
--bound 0
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^file .* line \d+: `Verilog::\$root\.main\.i' has multiple drivers$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
verilog_rtl_buildert::commit (src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp) tracks writes
to every symbol assigned in an always block, including elaboration-only
'integer' loop counters, and rejects a counter shared by two blocks as a
driver conflict. verilog_synthesist::assignment_rec in
verilog_synthesis.cpp has an analogous bug, already fixed by exempting
'integer'-typed symbols (PR #2049, "don't treat 'integer' loop counters
as driver conflicts"); the same
exemption is still missing from the verilog_rtl.cpp builder used here.
